  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Preheat the oven to 220C, fan-forced. Line a large oven tray with baking paper. Combine the dukkah, 1 tbs olive oil and 1 tsp honey in a bowl and season with salt and pepper.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2822254/photos/large/333715_1-8158fcf9a89688f5d7cbbb3a5f56de86.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake pita: Put 2 pita on the lined tray and brush with the dukkah mixture. Bake for 6 mins or until golden and crisp.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2822255/photos/large/333715_2-850f5fbc8cd6dd7c50e02cbe4a9f9753.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Prep cucumber: Meanwhile, thinly slice the cucumber. Put in a bowl, drizzle with 1 tsp white wine vinegar and season with salt and pepper.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2822256/photos/large/333715_3-2c58eb29d3998115e8ac9b804a063ea5.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fill pita: Remove the tray from the oven and spread the pita with the hummus. Add the cucumber and spinach to one side. Crumble over the feta and scatter with the sunflower seeds (see Make it yours).",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2822257/photos/large/333715_4-67748553711fa9d215a8955141720ff9.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Fold the pita over to enclose the filling, gently pushing down to flatten. Cut in half, then divide among plates and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2822258/photos/large/333715_5-5ee6b0c70f3ef80250ea13bfc891742f.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it yours: Like your seeds extra crunchy? Put them in a cold frypan over medium heat. Toast, tossing, for 3-4 mins until evenly golden. Remove from the pan and cool slightly before adding to your pita.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2822259/photos/large/333715_6-6008943387a372362a097cc2b5e7fe2e.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
